      "message": "I was thinking we could guard this additionally with CONFIG_LD_IS_LLD, but:\n1. ld.bfd also supports -z notext\n2. this bug is exacerbated by ld.bfd defaulting to -z text, while ld.lld is stricter in that it defaults to -z notext.\n\nNote: this patch is strictly for linking 32b x86 w/ LLD in 5.4.\n\nThis is a much simpler fix than trying to backport this 7 patch series:\nhttps://lore.kernel.org/lkml/20200717201801.3661843-2-nivedita@alum.mit.edu/T/#u",
